description:
When I  got a `ui.input_text()` that is only shown in some situations (e.g. when a checkbox was ticked, the input validation works as expected when it's shown for the first time. When the box is unticked and ticked again though, the validation is not run (see MWE and screenshots below). Is there a way to manually trigger the validation again so that the message is shown again? I tried `iv.validate()` but that didn't change the display.

```python
from shiny import App, ui, render, req
from shiny_validate import InputValidator, check

app_ui = ui.page_fluid(
    ui.card(
        ui.input_checkbox("checkbox", "show input"),
        ui.output_ui("name_field"),
        ui.output_text("output"),
    )
)


def server(input, output, session):
    iv = InputValidator()

    iv.add_rule("name", check.required())
    iv.enable()

    @render.text
    def output():
        req(iv.is_valid())
        return f"Nice to meet you, {input.name()}!"

    @render.ui
    def name_field():
        if input.checkbox():
            return ui.input_text("name", "What is your name?")


app = App(app_ui, server)
```

